- How does this adapt if negative weights are allowed but no negative cycles exist?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to frame a sign-assignment problem as a DP and implement both memoization and tabulation, a common interview pattern.

## Key Concepts
- DP state reduction to subset sum
- Space optimization with a 1D array
- Memoization vs bottom-up trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Tabulation and Memo versions
function countTargetSumTab(nums, S) {
  const total = nums.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);
  if (Math.abs(S) > total || (total+S)%2 !== 0) return 0;
  const target = (total+S)/2;
  const dp = Array(target+1).fill(0);
  dp[0] = 1;
  for (const n of nums) {
    for (let t = target; t >= n; t--) dp[t] += dp[t-n];
  }
  return dp[target];
}

function countTargetSumMemo(nums, S) {
  const total = nums.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);
  if (Math.abs(S) > total || (total+S)%2 !== 0) return 0;
  const target = (total+S)/2;
  const memo = new Map();
  function dfs(i, sum){
    if (sum > target) return 0;
    if (i === nums.length) return sum === target ? 1 : 0;
    const key = i+':'+sum;
    if (memo.has(key)) return memo.get(key);
    const res = dfs(i+1, sum+nums[i]) + dfs(i+1, sum);
    memo.set(key, res);
    return res;
  }
  return dfs(0,0);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to design augmented self-balancing BSTs for dynamic range queries—a common requirement in analytics and data processing applications.

## Key Concepts

- **AVL balancing**: Maintaining height balance factor (|left.height - right.height| ≤ 1) through rotations
- **Augmented BST data**: Storing additional aggregate information (cnt, sum) at each node
- **Range query on BST**: Using the BST property to efficiently prune irrelevant subtrees
- **Correctness and complexity analysis**: Ensuring O(log n) operations and verifying invariants

## Code Example

```javascript
class Node {
  constructor(key) {
    this.key = key;
    this.cnt = 1;
    this.height = 1;
    this.left = null;
    this.right = null;
    this.sum = key;
  }
}

function getHeight(node) { return node ? node.height : 0; }
function getSum(node) { return node ? node.sum : 0; }
function update(node) {
  node.height = 1 + Math.max(getHeight(node.left), getHeight(node.right));
  node.sum = getSum(node.left) + node.key * node.cnt + getSum(node.right);
}

function rightRotate(y) {
  const x = y.left;
  y.left = x.right;
  x.right = y;
  update(y);
  update(x);
  return x;
}

function rangeSum(node, a, b) {
  if (!node) return 0;
  if (node.key < a) return rangeSum(node.right, a, b);
  if (node.key > b) return rangeSum(node.left, a, b);
  return getSum(node.left) + node.key * node.cnt + rangeSum(node.right, a, b);
}
```

